man\",\"biography\":\"The driving force behind Suzlon's growth since its establishment in 1995, Tulsi Tanti's vision and strategic acumen transformed Suzlon and made it a global powerhouse in the energy sector. A world-renowned expert on renewable energy, Tulsi Tanti believed in creating sustainable businesses and a sustainable world through energy independence and security.\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/tulsi_tanti_046356bb4b.webp?v=2026-09-25T17%3A20%3A26.133Z\",\"mobileImageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/tulsi_tanti_046356bb4b.webp?v=2026-09-25T17%3A20%3A26.133Z\",\"imageAlt\":\"Tulsi Tanti\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Explore His Legacy\",\"ctaHref\":\"/about-us/founders-legacy/wind-man\"}}]]}],\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\",\"$L2d\"]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2e:I[26448,[\"/_next/static/chunks/11urp~c3h48hr.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3j1t.f~n0_..js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0i1xn6azr-jv8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0vlamz72s5jd9.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0ryfelz1efv9f.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0wbw_aigm92.r.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0nqns4awvpb~z.js\"],\"default\"]\n2f:I[572186,[\"/_next/static/chunks/11urp~c3h48hr.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3j1t.f~n0_..js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0i1xn6azr-jv8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0vlamz72s5jd9.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0ryfelz1efv9f.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0wbw_aigm92.r.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0nqns4awvpb~z.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[722510,[\"/_next/static/chunks/11urp~c3h48hr.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3j1t.f~n0_..js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0i1xn6azr-jv8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0vlamz72s5jd9.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0ryfelz1efv9f.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0wbw_aigm92.r.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0nqns4awvpb~z.js\"],\"default\"]\n35:I[133549,[\"/_next/static/chunks/11urp~c3h48hr.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3j1t.f~n0_..js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0i1xn6azr-jv8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0vlamz72s5jd9.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0ryfelz1efv9f.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0wbw_aigm92.r.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0nqns4awvpb~z.js\"],\"default\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:[\"$\",\"$L2e\",null,{\"data\":{\"title\":\"Group Executive council\",\"members\":[{\"id\":\"Vinod  Tanti\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/vinod_tanti_6e57325219.png?v=2026-09-02T12%3A50%3A54.042Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Vinod  \",\"Tanti\"],\"role\":\"Chairman and Managing Director, Suzlon Group\",\"bioParagraphs\":[\"Vinod Tanti, brother of Tulsi Tanti and the eldest among the remaining siblings, is a founding member of Suzlon Energy Limited. He has a Bachelor's Degree in Civil Engineering and extensive experience of over three decades managing various key functions at Suzlon. With a strong techno-commercial background, he has handled diverse portfolios, like wind resource assessment, acquisition, product design, prototyping, comprehensive supply management, project execution, and lifecycle management through operations and maintenance services.\",\"Vinod Tanti brings to Suzlon his vast experience of the complete wind energy value chain as well as his process-centricity and drive for innovation. Suzlon established and continues to maintain its technology and service leadership in India under his supervision.\"]},{\"id\":\"Girish  Tanti\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/girish_tanti_f9a438f69e.png?v=2026-09-02T12%3A52%3A16.707Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Girish  \",\"Tanti\"],\"role\":\"Co-founder, Suzlon Group\",\"bioParagraphs\":[\"Girish Tanti, brother of Tulsi Tanti and youngest among the remaining siblings, is also a founding member of Suzlon Energy Limited. He has a Bachelor's Degree in Electronics \u0026 Communication Engineering and holds a Master's Degree in Business Administration from the United Kingdom. He brings to Suzlon an extensive experience of nearly three decades in renewables and international business.\",\"Girish Tanti holds a unique blend of understanding the dynamics of technology and strong business acumen. Over the years, he has played several key roles, including incubating the renewable energy business in 1995, establishing technology development centres in Europe and India, setting up the global supply chain, developing wind markets across India, establishing global business operations, and spearheading corporate development activities.\",\"He also led various service functions, such as human resources, information technology, communications, and CSR. He has been instrumental in Suzlon's rise to becoming the only wind energy player from a developing nation to rank among the top five worldwide.\"]},{\"id\":\"JP  Chalasani\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/leadership_jp_chalasani_gec_44f20bd14f.jpg?v=2026-09-02T12%3A53%3A01.635Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"JP  \",\"Chalasani\"],\"role\":\"Member, Group Executive Council\",\"bioParagraphs\":[\"JP Chalasani joined the Suzlon Group as Chief Executive Officer in April 2016. He currently serves as a Member of the Group Executive Council and plays a key role in driving strategic initiatives across the Group. Distinguished for his project management and people leadership skills, he brings to the company more than four decades of experience working in the Indian power sector, particularly with organisations such as NTPC, Reliance Power, and Punj Lloyd.\",\"JP Chalasani holds a Bachelor's Degree in Mechanical Engineering, which supports his strong understanding of project execution, engineering operations, and industrial processes.\"]},{\"id\":\"Kirti  Vagadia\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Kirti_Vagadia_400x533_2a0e891f78.png?v=2026-09-02T12%3A53%3A27.145Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Kirti  \",\"Vagadia\"],\"role\":\"Member, Group Executive Council\",\"bioParagraphs\":[\"Kirti Vagadia is a Finance veteran with nearly four decades of experience in strategic and corporate finance. He has been associated with Suzlon since its inception and has played an integral role in shaping its growth from a startup to a global leader.\",\"Kirti Vagadia brings deep expertise in financial planning, capital allocation, mergers \u0026 acquisitions, and navigating market cycles, with a strong focus on sustainable value creation and governance. Formerly Group Chief Financial Officer till September 2019 and later a strategic advisor for five years, he has worked closely with Suzlon's Founder on strategy, capital structure, and business transformation. A Chartered Accountant with a Master's in Commerce, he possesses a strong network amongst leading financial institutions, investment bankers, and advisors.\"]}]}}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2b:[\"$\",\"$L2f\",null,{\"data\":{\"title\":\"Executive Management Council\",\"members\":[{\"id\":\"Ajay Kapur\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/ajay_kapur_400x533_2f2d091a22.jpg?v=2026-09-02T12%3A58%3A46.248Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Ajay   \",\"Kapur\"],\"role\":\"Chief Executive Officer, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"Ajay Kapur plays a critical role in driving scale, growth, and business transformation across the Group. He brings over three decades of expertise across the Cement, Construction, Power, and Heavy Metals sectors, as well as over a decade of independent CEO leadership experience with large, listed firms. Prior to this role, he served as Managing Director of Ambuja Cements Limited (an Adani Group company) and has been actively involved with industry forums such as CII, FICCI, and ASSOCHAM. He holds a degree in Economics and an MBA from K. J. Somaiya Institute of Management, and he is an alumnus of the Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania.\"},{\"id\":\"Rahul Jain\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/rahul_jain_400x533_43bf58a89c.jpg?v=2026-09-02T12%3A59%3A46.365Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Rahul \",\"Jain\"],\"role\":\"Chief Financial Officer, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"Rahul Jain plays a critical role in scaling new markets, technologies, and opportunities for the Suzlon Group. He is a veteran of corporate finance with extensive experience in leading financial transformation, streamlining systems, leveraging technology, and strengthening financial discipline to support the organic and inorganic growth of his organisations. A Chartered Accountant, he is seasoned in identifying new avenues and unlocking capital allocation, among others. Rahul Jain has previously dedicated nearly two decades to SRF Limited and a decade to Jubilant Organosys Limited.\"},{\"id\":\"Anjali Byce\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Anjali_Byce_400x533_d556b83e63.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A01%3A08.798Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Anjali \",\"Byce\"],\"role\":\"Chief Human Resources Officer, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"Anjali Byce safeguards Suzlon's culture, oversees people transformation programs, and drives diversity initiatives to maintain a high-performing, inclusive workplace. She brings nearly three decades of experience in the human resources, manufacturing, automotive, insurance, and finance sectors. Her people transformation initiatives have earned her several prestigious titles, including CHRO of the Year 2020 and 100 Most Talented Global HR Leaders. Anjali holds a Bachelor's Degree in Psychology and two Master's Degrees in Psychology and Human Resources \u0026 Marketing. Previously, she worked with respected companies, such as Tata Motors, Cummins, and Allianz Bajaj Life Insurance Co.\"},{\"id\":\"Gurpratap Boparai\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Gurpratap_Boparai_400x533_951b222f7e.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A44%3A24.376Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Gurpratap \",\"Boparai\"],\"role\":\"Chief Executive Officer, Manufacturing Business\",\"profileBio\":\"Gurpratap Boparai oversees the end-to-end operational excellence journey of the Manufacturing Business, a crucial business division, while spearheading its digitisation. A veteran of the automobile and engineering sectors, he brings over three decades of experience in manufacturing operations, greenfield projects, company restructuring, and financial management. He holds a Bachelor’s Degree in Mechanical Engineering and an MBA in Marketing \u0026 Finance from XLRI Jamshedpur. Over the course of his career, he has also held leadership roles across global manufacturing organisations.\"},{\"id\":\"Sandeep Chowdhury\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Sandeep_Chowdhury_400x533_4d5f28fee9.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A45%3A52.360Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Sandeep \",\"Chowdhury\"],\"role\":\"General Counsel, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"Sandeep Chowdhury is responsible for strengthening internal governance, fostering stakeholder engagement, and ensuring robust legal compliance across the Suzlon Group. He brings extensive global expertise in litigation, advisory, mergers \u0026 acquisitions, labour, intellectual property, and compliance to the Group. He holds an LL.B. (Hons) from Calcutta University and was previously associated with organisations with global repute.\"},{\"id\":\"Bernhard Telgmann\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/leadership_bernhard_telgmann_emc_13c9be040c.jpg?v=2026-09-02T13%3A46%3A24.849Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Bernhard \",\"Telgmann\"],\"role\":\"President - Technology\",\"profileBio\":\"Bernhard Telgmann joined Suzlon in 2017 and leads technology development for the Group. He has nearly three decades of experience in engineering thermal power plants, consulting in fuel cells, and wind energy. He also brings expertise in global technology-driven plant engineering and construction to the Group. Bernhard Telgmann is a strategist with a keen sense of product innovation and growth opportunities. He leads the development and launch of new products and technologies, ensuring faster time-to-market and lower costs. His expertise also covers product development, engineering, and project execution in the system and solution business. Prior to Suzlon, he held leadership roles in IAC and Siemens.\"},{\"id\":\"Kamlesh Bhadani\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Kamlesh_Bhadani_400x533_5140d897fe.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A46%3A47.010Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Kamlesh \",\"Bhadani\"],\"role\":\"Managing Director, SE Forge Limited\",\"profileBio\":\"Kamlesh Bhadani oversees customer-focused research and development, strategic advisory, and growth planning. Having been with Suzlon since its founding years, he has played a pivotal role in the company's global expansion in China and contributed to several milestone projects for Suzlon and SE Forge. With extensive experience across the Energy, Oil, Gas, and Manufacturing sectors, he continues to focus on customer-centric innovation and sustainability-driven growth.\"},{\"id\":\"Ashok Ramachandran\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Ashok_Ramachandran_400x533_0d58690291.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A49%3A14.164Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Ashok \",\"Ramachandran\"],\"role\":\"President - India Business\",\"profileBio\":\"Ashok Ramachandran strengthens growth and execution capabilities to drive Suzlon's wind-first, full-stack renewable energy ambitions. He has over two decades of global leadership experience and a forward-looking strategic acumen in energy, industrial products, and vertical mobility. He holds a Master's Degree in Industrial Engineering from Swinburne University and is seasoned in M\u0026A, turnaround, business transformation, and cross-cultural leadership. Over the course of his career, Ashok has been associated with the likes of JSW Energy, Schindler, and REE Corporation, where he played key roles in shaping a strategic roadmap from ~5 GW to ~30 GW capacity, leading business turnarounds in underperforming markets, and heading Southeast Asia's most complex multi-sector portfolios for a USD 1.5 billion company, respectively.\"},{\"id\":\"Manjari  Upadhye\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/manjari_upadhye_dd912958f1.png?v=2026-09-24T09%3A31%3A03.607Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Manjari  \",\"Upadhye\"],\"role\":\"President - RE Asset Management Services (AMS)\",\"profileBio\":\"Manjari Upadhye leads Suzlon's RE Asset Management Services (RE AMS) business, with a strong focus on customer-centricity, service excellence, and long-term value creation. She brings nearly three decades of expertise in strategy, innovation, marketing, and P\u0026L management across various sectors in India, Asia Pacific, and the USA. She has previously been associated with prestigious brands like Mahindra \u0026 Mahindra, Welspun, Amazon, and Mondelez in various leadership capacities. She holds an MBA in Marketing and Finance from FMS, Delhi, and is seasoned in consumer behaviour, brand building, and services management.\"}]}}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"31:T445,Girish Tanti, brother of Tulsi Tanti and youngest among the remaining siblings, is also a founding member of Suzlon Energy Limited. He has a Bachelor's Degree in Electronics \u0026 Communication Engineering and holds a Master's Degree in Business Administration from the United Kingdom. He brings to Suzlon an extensive experience of nearly three decades in renewables and international business.Girish Tanti holds a unique blend of understanding the dynamics of technology and strong business acumen. Over the years, he has played several key roles, including incubating the renewable energy business in 1995, establishing technology development centres in Europe and India, setting up the global supply chain, developing wind markets across India, establishing global business operations, and spearheading corporate development activities.He also led various service functions, such as human resources, information technology, communications, and CSR. He has been instrumental in Suzlon's rise to becoming the only wind energy player from a developing nation to rank among the top five worldwide.32:T500,Pranav Tanti is the eldest child of Tulsi Tanti. With over two decades of experience in international business, he possesses extensive expertise in the renewable energy industry. During his diverse global experience, he worked in some of the world’s major business hubs, including India, China, the United States, and Hong Kong. Most recently, he served as the Chief Executive Officer of Skeiron Renewable Energy, a company he founded that invested in and managed a portfolio of nearly 400 MW of wind turbine assets. Pranav Tanti spearheaded fundraising from two Hong Kong-based private equity firms. At the market peak in 2018, he successfully led the exit of the portfolio, valued at US$ 500 million. Prior to this, he held various executive roles at the Suzlon Group’s Chicago and India offices. He also held positions at Merrill Lynch and CLSA, working in investment banking and equity research in Hong Kong and Beijing. Currently, he leads efforts to develop large-scale utility projects for Green Hydrogen and Green Ammonia in North America and Asia. He holds a Master’s Degree in Business Administration from the University of Chicago Booth School of Business and a dual honours degree in Business Administration and Finance from Keele University, the United Kingdom.33:T5f8,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Sameer Shah serves as an Independent Director of the Suzlon Group. He has over four decades of experience spanning finance, banking, governance, and strategy across diverse geographies and industry verticals. In his previous role, he served as the Chief Financial Officer and Head of Information and Communications Technology at a petroleum, chemicals, and mining company for five years. Prior to that, he worked at Deutsche Bank for 13 years as a Managing Director, heading the Equity Services Business for Asia Pacific and the Arabian Gulf. He also led the Corporate Banking division for Western India from 2009 to 2011. He previously worked with SABIC, Ontario Hydro (Hydro One), and Tata Consultancy Services. Mr. Shah is a qualified Treasurer with the Association of Corporate Treasurers based in London, United Kingdom. Currently, he works as an independent Strategic Planning and Finance Consultant and collaborates with various non-profit organisations in leadership and advisory roles. His work includes contributions to organisations such as Mercy Ships, Pacific Opera Victoria, Victoria Literacy Connection, and Sidney Classical Orchestra in Canada. He has also actively supported initiatives at Chinmaya Mission, the Sujaya Foundation, Jeevan Vikas Ganga Trust, and United Way. He holds a Bachelor’s Degree in Science with honours from the University of Mumbai, a Master of Business Administration from the University of Rochester, New York, and a Diploma in Securities Law from the Government Law College, Mumbai."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"34:T5c3,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Seemantinee Khot serves as an Independent Director of the Suzlon Group. She brings over four decades of experience in sustainable development and has worked with domestic and international organisations, including the Food and Agriculture Organisation of the United Nations (FAO), Swiss Development Corporation, International Fund for Agricultural Development, and various bilateral aid projects. She has served on and continues to serve on the boards of multiple listed/unlisted companies, not-for-profits, microfinance institutions, and farmer-producer organisations. She is dedicated to agro-based livelihoods, rural development, and women’s empowerment through bodies such as Participatory Research in Asia and BAIF Development Research Foundation. She has been instrumental in introducing gendered situation analysis and responding to class and caste inequities in governmental and non-governmental projects. Seemantinee Khto has worked across all continents as a Senior Evaluation Specialist for the UN Food and Agriculture Organisation. She is a Partner at CHHAYA Strategic Advisors LLP, a founding member of ‘Every Woman Everywhere’ of Harvard Business School, and part of ‘Consult for Women’s Land and Resource Rights.’ In 2023, she was honoured with the prestigious Iconic Women Directors Awards 2023 for Greater Social Impact. She holds a Bachelor of Arts in Psychology and a Master’s Degree in Social Work from the Tata Institute of Social Sciences."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2c:[\"$\",\"$L30\",null,{\"data\":{\"title\":\"Board of Directors\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Directorship in Indian Companies\",\"ctaHref\":\"/pdf/about/Directorships-in-Indian-Companies.pdf\",\"members\":[{\"id\":\"Vinod Tanti\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Vinod_Tanti_fba57c5c4e.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A53%3A01.870Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Vinod   \",\"Tanti\"],\"role\":\"Chairman and Managing Director, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"Vinod Tanti, brother of Tulsi Tanti and the eldest among the remaining siblings, is a founding member of Suzlon Energy Limited. He has a Bachelor's Degree in Civil Engineering and extensive experience of over three decades managing various key functions at Suzlon. With a strong techno-commercial background, he has handled diverse portfolios, like wind resource assessment, acquisition, product design, prototyping, comprehensive supply management, project execution, and lifecycle management through operations and maintenance services.Vinod Tanti brings to Suzlon his vast experience of the complete wind energy value chain as well as his process-centricity and drive for innovation. Suzlon established and continues to maintain its technology and service leadership in India under his supervision.\"},{\"id\":\"Girish Tanti\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Girish_Tanti_800f45b3b8.png?v=2026-09-08T11%3A17%3A55.828Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Girish   \",\"Tanti\"],\"role\":\"Co-founder, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"$31\"},{\"id\":\"Pranav Tanti\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Pranav_Tanti_e20e417d01.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A54%3A18.452Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Pranav   \",\"Tanti\"],\"role\":\"Non-Executive Director, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"$32\"},{\"id\":\"Sameer Shah\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Sameer_Shah_9323d75f12.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A54%3A45.587Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Sameer   \",\"Shah\"],\"role\":\"Independent Director, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"$33\"},{\"id\":\"Seemantinee Khot\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Seemantinee_Khot_86e083ccb7.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A55%3A07.521Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Seemantinee   \",\"Khot\"],\"role\":\"Independent Director, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"$34\"},{\"id\":\"Girish Vanvari\",\"imageSrc\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/uploads/Girish_Vanvari_3d8eba1660.png?v=2026-09-02T13%3A55%3A32.190Z\",\"imageAlt\":null,\"nameLines\":[\"Girish   \",\"Vanvari\"],\"role\":\"Independent Director, Suzlon Group\",\"profileBio\":\"Girish Vanvari serves as an Independent Director of the Suzlon Group. He is a Chartered Accountant with over three decades of experience across taxation, corporate finance, M\u0026A, valuations, corporate restructuring, and corporate governance. In the boardroom, he is known for bringing financial discipline, oversight, regulatory insight, and practical business judgment, and for contributing across audit committee deliberations, risk management, capital allocation, RPT reviews, and governance frameworks.\"}]}}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2d:[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"data\":{\"title\":\"Committees of Board\",\"committees\":[{\"name\":\"Audit Committee\",\"memberLines\":[\"Girish Vanvari (Chairman),\",\"Vinod Tanti,\",\"Sameer Shah\"]},{\"name\":\"Stakeholders Relationship Committee\",\"memberLines\":[\"Seemantinee Khot (Chairperson),\",\"Vinod Tanti,\",\"Girish Tanti\"]},{\"name\":\"Nomination and Remuneration Committee\",\"memberLines\":[\"Sameer Shah (Chairman),\",\"Seemantinee Khot,\",\"Pranav Tanti\"]},{\"name\":\"CSR \u0026 ESG Committee\",\"memberLines\":[\"Seemantinee Khot (Chairperson),\",\"Girish Tanti,\",\"Vinod Tanti\"]},{\"name\":\"Securities Issue Committee\",\"memberLines\":[\"Vinod Tanti (Chairman),\",\"Girish Tanti\"]},{\"name\":\"Risk Management Committee\",\"memberLines\":[\"Vinod Tanti (Chairman),\",\"Ajay Kapur,\",\"Girish Vanvari\"]}]}}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"36:I[27201,[\"/_next/static/chunks/11urp~c3h48hr.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3j1t.f~n0_..js\"],\"IconMark\"]\nb:null\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"10:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"About Suzlon | Creators of Good Energy\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Learn about Suzlon - creators of good energy with 21,500 MW installed globally across wind, solar, and storage solutions.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"manifest\",\"href\":\"/favicon/site.webmanifest\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"4\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/about-us/leadership/\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"About Suzlon | Creators of Good Energy\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"Learn about Suzlon - creators of good energy with 21,500 MW installed globally across wind, solar, and storage solutions.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"property\":\"og:url\",\"content\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/about-us/leadership/\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"property\":\"og:site_name\",\"content\":\"Suzlon Energy\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"property\":\"og:locale\",\"content\":\"en_IN\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"property\":\"og:image\",\"content\":\"https://www.suzlon.com/images/meta-image/Meta-Image-1920x1080.jpg\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"property\":\"og:image:al